<tool id="3dtrees_sidecar" name="3Dtrees: Sidecar" version="@TOOL_VERSION@+galaxy@VERSION_SUFFIX@" profile="24.2">
    <description>Store method results as sidecars and assemble point clouds</description>
    <macros>
        <token name="@TOOL_VERSION@">0.1.0</token>
        <token name="@VERSION_SUFFIX@">0</token>
        <xml name="generation">
            <param argument="--generation" type="text" label="Standard generation id" help="Which standardization the points come from. The platform fills this in; by hand, use any UUID and the same one for every task">
                <validator type="regex" message="A generation UUID is required">^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}\Z</validator>
            </param>
        </xml>
        <xml name="base">
            <param argument="--base" type="data" format="laz" label="Standard base point cloud" help="The standardized point cloud of one item; its collection element identifier (or dataset name outside a collection) must be a positive numeric item id"/>
        </xml>
        <xml name="sidecars">
            <repeat name="sidecars" title="Sidecar" help="Add one per method result to include; none gives the points only">
                <param argument="--sidecar" type="data" format="parquet" label="Sidecar"/>
            </repeat>
        </xml>
    </macros>
    <requirements>
        <container type="docker">ghcr.io/3dtrees-earth/3dtrees_sidecar:@TOOL_VERSION@</container>
    </requirements>
    <version_command>python /src/run.py --version</version_command>
    <command detect_errors="exit_code"><![CDATA[
        #import re
        #if $operation.task == 'export'
            #set $item_id = str($operation.enriched.element_identifier)
        #else
            #set $item_id = str($operation.base.element_identifier)
        #end if
        #if not re.match(r'^[0-9]+\Z', $item_id)
            #set $item_id = 'invalid'
        #end if
        python -u /src/run.py '$operation.task'
        --generation '$operation.generation'
        --item '$item_id'
        #if $operation.task == 'export'
            --enriched '$operation.enriched'
            --columns '$operation.columns'
            --output sidecar.parquet
        #else
            --base '$operation.base'
            #for $selected in $operation.sidecars
                --sidecar '$selected.sidecar'
            #end for
            #if $operation.task == 'assemble'
                --output member.laz
            #else
                --member '$operation.member'
            #end if
        #end if
        --report '$report'
    ]]></command>
    <inputs>
        <conditional name="operation">
            <param name="task" type="select" label="Task">
                <option value="export">Export: cut one method's new columns out of its result</option>
                <option value="assemble">Assemble: build the download point cloud from base and sidecars</option>
                <option value="check">Check: verify a published download point cloud</option>
            </param>
            <when value="export">
                <param argument="--enriched" type="data" format="laz" label="Method result point cloud" help="One item's method output; its collection element identifier (or dataset name outside a collection) must be a positive numeric item id"/>
                <param argument="--columns" type="text" label="Columns to keep" help="Comma-separated names of the columns to store, for example PredInstance_SAT,PredSemantic_SAT. Every other added column is left out with a warning.">
                    <validator type="regex" message="Comma-separated column names without spaces">^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(,[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)*\Z</validator>
                </param>
                <expand macro="generation"/>
            </when>
            <when value="assemble">
                <expand macro="base"/>
                <expand macro="generation"/>
                <expand macro="sidecars"/>
            </when>
            <when value="check">
                <expand macro="base"/>
                <expand macro="generation"/>
                <expand macro="sidecars"/>
                <param argument="--member" type="data" format="laz" label="Point cloud to verify" help="The download point cloud made by assemble"/>
            </when>
        </conditional>
    </inputs>
    <outputs>
        <data name="sidecar" format="parquet" from_work_dir="sidecar.parquet" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: Sidecar">
            <filter>operation['task'] == 'export'</filter>
        </data>
        <data name="member" format="laz" from_work_dir="member.laz" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: Point cloud">
            <filter>operation['task'] == 'assemble'</filter>
        </data>
        <data name="report" format="json" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}: Report"/>
    </outputs>
    <tests>
        <!-- Export both SAT columns and verify the actual Parquet values. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="task" value="export"/>
                <param name="enriched" value="sat/11353" ftype="laz"/>
                <param name="columns" value="PredInstance_SAT,PredSemantic_SAT"/>
                <param name="generation" value="0b0a6f1e-6a4e-4d8e-9f3c-1d2e3f4a5b6c"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="sidecar" file="sat.parquet" ftype="parquet"/>
            <output name="report" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="item_id" value="11353"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="points" value="500"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="generation" value="&quot;0b0a6f1e-6a4e-4d8e-9f3c-1d2e3f4a5b6c&quot;"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="dimensions" value="{&quot;PredInstance_SAT&quot;: &quot;&lt;u4&quot;, &quot;PredSemantic_SAT&quot;: &quot;&lt;u4&quot;}"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="dropped" value="[]"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="contract" value="&quot;3dtrees-scientific-sidecar-proof-v2&quot;"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Export only the requested method from a combined result. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="task" value="export"/>
                <param name="enriched" value="legacy/11353" ftype="laz"/>
                <param name="columns" value="PredInstance_SAT,PredSemantic_SAT"/>
                <param name="generation" value="0b0a6f1e-6a4e-4d8e-9f3c-1d2e3f4a5b6c"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="sidecar" file="sat.parquet" ftype="parquet"/>
            <output name="report" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="dimensions" value="{&quot;PredInstance_SAT&quot;: &quot;&lt;u4&quot;, &quot;PredSemantic_SAT&quot;: &quot;&lt;u4&quot;}"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="dropped" value="[&quot;PredInstance_FM&quot;, &quot;PredScore_FM&quot;, &quot;PredSemantic_FM&quot;]"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="points" value="500"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <assert_stderr>
                <has_text text="columns not kept"/>
            </assert_stderr>
        </test>
        <!-- Reject columns absent from the method output. -->
        <test expect_failure="true" expect_exit_code="2">
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="task" value="export"/>
                <param name="enriched" value="11353" ftype="laz"/>
                <param name="columns" value="PredInstance_SAT"/>
                <param name="generation" value="0b0a6f1e-6a4e-4d8e-9f3c-1d2e3f4a5b6c"/>
            </conditional>
            <assert_stderr>
                <has_text text="Requested columns are not in the output: ['PredInstance_SAT']"/>
            </assert_stderr>
        </test>
        <!-- No sidecars preserves every byte of the standardized point cloud. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="task" value="assemble"/>
                <param name="base" value="11353" ftype="laz"/>
                <param name="generation" value="0b0a6f1e-6a4e-4d8e-9f3c-1d2e3f4a5b6c"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="member" file="base.laz" ftype="laz"/>
            <output name="report" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="item_id" value="11353"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="points" value="500"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="dimensions" value="[]"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Assemble one method and verify its values and the base fields. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="task" value="assemble"/>
                <param name="base" value="11353" ftype="laz"/>
                <param name="generation" value="0b0a6f1e-6a4e-4d8e-9f3c-1d2e3f4a5b6c"/>
                <repeat name="sidecars">
                    <param name="sidecar" value="sat.parquet" ftype="parquet"/>
                </repeat>
            </conditional>
            <output name="member" file="sat.laz" ftype="laz"/>
            <output name="report" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="points" value="500"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="dimensions" value="[&quot;PredInstance_SAT&quot;, &quot;PredSemantic_SAT&quot;]"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Assemble two methods and verify every output byte. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="2">
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="task" value="assemble"/>
                <param name="base" value="11353" ftype="laz"/>
                <param name="generation" value="0b0a6f1e-6a4e-4d8e-9f3c-1d2e3f4a5b6c"/>
                <repeat name="sidecars">
                    <param name="sidecar" value="sat.parquet" ftype="parquet"/>
                </repeat>
                <repeat name="sidecars">
                    <param name="sidecar" value="forestmamba.parquet" ftype="parquet"/>
                </repeat>
            </conditional>
            <output name="member" file="member_both.laz" ftype="laz"/>
            <output name="report" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="points" value="500"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="dimensions" value="[&quot;PredInstance_FM&quot;, &quot;PredInstance_SAT&quot;, &quot;PredScore_FM&quot;, &quot;PredSemantic_FM&quot;, &quot;PredSemantic_SAT&quot;]"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Check a point cloud without sidecars. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="task" value="check"/>
                <param name="base" value="11353" ftype="laz"/>
                <param name="generation" value="0b0a6f1e-6a4e-4d8e-9f3c-1d2e3f4a5b6c"/>
                <param name="member" value="base.laz" ftype="laz"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="report" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="contract" value="&quot;3dtrees-sidecar-check-v1&quot;"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="item_id" value="11353"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="points" value="500"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="generation" value="&quot;0b0a6f1e-6a4e-4d8e-9f3c-1d2e3f4a5b6c&quot;"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="sidecars" value="[]"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Check a point cloud with both methods. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="task" value="check"/>
                <param name="base" value="11353" ftype="laz"/>
                <param name="generation" value="0b0a6f1e-6a4e-4d8e-9f3c-1d2e3f4a5b6c"/>
                <repeat name="sidecars">
                    <param name="sidecar" value="sat.parquet" ftype="parquet"/>
                </repeat>
                <repeat name="sidecars">
                    <param name="sidecar" value="forestmamba.parquet" ftype="parquet"/>
                </repeat>
                <param name="member" value="member_both.laz" ftype="laz"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="report" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="contract" value="&quot;3dtrees-sidecar-check-v1&quot;"/>
                    <has_json_property_with_value property="points" value="500"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Reject a member with extra unselected columns. -->
        <test expect_failure="true" expect_exit_code="2">
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="task" value="check"/>
                <param name="base" value="11353" ftype="laz"/>
                <param name="generation" value="0b0a6f1e-6a4e-4d8e-9f3c-1d2e3f4a5b6c"/>
                <param name="member" value="sat.laz" ftype="laz"/>
            </conditional>
            <assert_stderr>
                <has_text text="Member dimensions differ from the selected sidecars"/>
            </assert_stderr>
        </test>
        <!-- Reject a member missing the selected columns. -->
        <test expect_failure="true" expect_exit_code="2">
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="task" value="check"/>
                <param name="base" value="11353" ftype="laz"/>
                <param name="generation" value="0b0a6f1e-6a4e-4d8e-9f3c-1d2e3f4a5b6c"/>
                <repeat name="sidecars">
                    <param name="sidecar" value="sat.parquet" ftype="parquet"/>
                </repeat>
                <repeat name="sidecars">
                    <param name="sidecar" value="forestmamba.parquet" ftype="parquet"/>
                </repeat>
                <param name="member" value="base.laz" ftype="laz"/>
            </conditional>
            <assert_stderr>
                <has_text text="Member dimensions differ from the selected sidecars"/>
            </assert_stderr>
        </test>
        <!-- Reject nonnumeric dataset names outside collections. -->
        <test expect_failure="true" expect_exit_code="2">
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="task" value="assemble"/>
                <param name="base" value="base.laz" ftype="laz"/>
                <param name="generation" value="0b0a6f1e-6a4e-4d8e-9f3c-1d2e3f4a5b6c"/>
            </conditional>
            <assert_stderr>
                <has_text text="item must be a positive Dataset item id"/>
            </assert_stderr>
        </test>
    </tests>
    <help><![CDATA[
**What it does**

Sidecar keeps each method's results apart from the point cloud. For every item
it stores only the columns you name (for example ``PredInstance_SAT``),
together with each point's number, in a small Parquet file: a *sidecar*. A
downloadable point cloud is built from the standardized file plus any chosen
sidecars, joined by point number, never by coordinates.

.. image:: $PATH_TO_IMAGES/sidecar_workflow.png
   :width: 100%

**Tasks**

- **Export**: turns one method's result into a sidecar. It stores only the
  columns named in *Columns to keep*, for example
  ``PredInstance_SAT,PredSemantic_SAT`` for SAT, ``species_id_SAT,species_prob_SAT``
  for a species result that also repeats SAT's columns, or one method's columns
  from an old file that holds several (run once per method). Every other column
  is left out and listed as a warning in the job's output and report. The
  result must hold the standardized points in the same order, because the
  sidecar is joined back by point number only.
- **Assemble**: builds one item's download point cloud: every field of the
  standardized file unchanged, plus the columns of each added *Sidecar*. Add one
  entry per method, from any method; none gives the points only. A sidecar is
  refused when its item, generation or point count differs.
- **Check**: rebuilds the download point cloud from the standardized file and
  the same sidecars, and compares it value by value with the file given as
  *Point cloud to verify*. The job fails on any difference.

**Several items**

Run every task on collections, one element per item, with the dataset item id
as element identifier (for example ``11353``). Galaxy then runs one job per
element and the item id is read from the element identifier. When assemble or
check gets the standardized collection and sidecar collections together, Galaxy
pairs their elements in collection order, so the collections must list the
same items in the same order. A mispaired sidecar is refused because its item
id does not match.

For a single dataset outside a collection, rename the method result (export)
or standardized base (assemble and check) to its positive numeric item id,
without a file extension. The item id is read from that dataset name.

Use one *Sidecar* entry per method and select that method's collection in
Galaxy's batch input mode. This lets Galaxy map the standardized file and each
method's sidecar together for every item.

**Standard generation id**

A UUID naming the standardization the points come from. The 3Dtrees platform
passes its own; by hand, use any UUID and the same one for export, assemble and
check. A sidecar with a different generation is refused.

**Outputs**

Export writes the sidecar, assemble the download LAZ. Every task also writes a
JSON report with point count, columns and SHA-256 hashes, so the 3Dtrees
platform can verify the results without downloading point clouds.
    ]]></help>
